{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"Whole-function compilation is about 1.3× faster locally, but its rewritten bias reductions miss the tolerance at large batch sizes. I’m narrowing compilation to the attention subgraph only; all four returned bias reductions and every projection remain the exact eager operators used by the reference. This should retain the safe numerical behavior while still fusing the five softmax-backward pointwise launches."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"env -u TORCH_LOGS python - <<'PY' 2>/dev/null\nimport torch, reference, time\nfrom torch.nn import functional as F\n\ndef attn(q,k,v,g,scale):\n s=torch.matmul(q,k.transpose(-2,-1))*scale\n p=F.softmax(s,dim=-1,dtype=torch.float32)\n c=torch.matmul(p,v)\n gp=torch.matmul(g,v.transpose(-2,-1))\n gv=torch.matmul(p.transpose(-2,-1),g)\n sm=(gp*p).sum(dim=-1,keepdim=True)\n gs=p*(gp-sm)\n gs=gs*scale\n gq=torch.matmul(gs,k)\n gk=torch.matmul(gs.transpose(-2,-1),q)\n return c,gq,gk,gv\nca=torch.compile(attn,fullgraph=True,dynamic=False,mode='default')\n\ndef cand(go,x,t,qw,qb,kw,kb,vw,vb,ow,ob,scale):\n B,N,D=x.shape; T=t.shape[1]; H=16; d=64\n q=F.linear(x,qw,qb).view(B,N,H,d).transpose(1,2); k=F.linear(t,kw,kb).view(B,T,H,d).transpose(1,2); v=F.linear(t,vw,vb).view(B,T,H,d).transpose(1,2)\n gc=go@ow; gch=gc.view(B,N,H,d).transpose(1,2)\n c,gq,gk,gv=ca(q,k,v,gch,scale)\n context=c.transpose(1,2).contiguous().view(B,N,D)\n gq=gq.transpose(1,2).contiguous().view(B,N,D); gk=gk.transpose(1,2).contiguous().view(B,T,D); gv=gv.transpose(1,2).contiguous().view(B,T,D)\n return (gq@qw,gk@kw+gv@vw,torch.einsum('bnd,bnk->dk',gq,x),gq.sum((0,1)),torch.einsum('bnd,bnk->dk',gk,t),gk.sum((0,1)),torch.einsum('bnd,bnk->dk',gv,t),gv.sum((0,1)),torch.einsum('bnd,bnk->dk',go,context),go.sum((0,1)))\nB,N,T,D=64,128,77,1024; shapes=[(B,N,D),(B,N,D),(B,T,D),(D,D),(D,),(D,D),(D,),(D,D),(D,),(D,D),(D,)]\nxs=[torch.randn(s,device='cuda')*.1 for s in shapes]\nt=time.time(); b=cand(*xs,.125); torch.cuda.synchronize(); print('compile',time.time()-t)\na=reference.run(*xs,.125); torch.cuda.synchronize()\nfor i,(x,y) in enumerate(zip(a,b)):\n e=(x-y).abs(); print(i,e.max().item(),torch.isclose(x,y,atol=2.989e-6,rtol=1.1920928955078125e-7).float().mean().item())\nfor _ in range(3): cand(*xs,.125)\ntorch.cuda.synchronize()\ndef bench(fn):\n vals=[]\n for _ in range(20):\n  s=torch.cuda.Event(True); e=torch